# EQUIVALENCE LEXICON - wordings YOU confirmed mean the same thing for your own work (system/engine/tools/claim_lexicon.py).
# Starts empty. Claude adds an entry only after asking you, e.g. "Three postings call it 'benchmark models'; your approved
# claim says 'challenger models'. Is 'benchmark models' an equally true description of what you did?" A yes adds an entry
# with today's date. From then on a resume may use either wording and the audit still passes. Entries without a
# 'confirmed' date are ignored. Never-claims stay forbidden whatever this file says.
#
# entries:
#   - approved: "challenger models"
#     equivalents: ["benchmark models"]
#     categories: []              # optional: lanes where the swap reads naturally; [] = any
#     confirmed: "2026-10-16"
entries: []
